cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use or cite this work, please cite it as below. A DOI will be added here once the first Zenodo-archived release is created."
title: "RoT — Return on Token: A Discussion Paper on Reducing Compute Waste from the Data Side"
authors:
  - family-names: "Yamada"
    given-names: "Masayuki"
type: software
repository-code: "https://github.com/beachcities/RoT"
license:
  - Apache-2.0
  - CC-BY-4.0
keywords:
  - open data
  - self-describing data
  - token efficiency
  - inference-time scaling
  - Return on Token
abstract: >-
  A discussion paper proposing Return on Token (ROT), an indicator that
  asks what was obtained for the tokens spent, and examines whether the
  self-description of data governs it. Includes a minimal benchmark that
  varies the level of self-description and measures token consumption
  per outcome, with results and full reproduction steps. The Japanese
  text (paper/return-on-token.md) is authoritative.
